Make Grid show the script. Repo /Users/x/Documents/edraft, branch rename/edraft, HEAD 02f4bb9 (clean tree — verify with git status first; never stage the xcscheme file, .codedirector/mcp.log, or the repo-root png files). Follow CLAUDE.md exactly: lock_draft → show me the Vibe Check → wait for my yes → lock_check + lock_activate → every change through run_locked → report. No commits, no co-author trailers.
The diagnosis is already measured — your job is the fix, not the search. In grid arrangement (apple/EDraftMacSurface/Sources/EDraftMacSurface/PageCanvasView.swift), the text view is hidden (line ~386) and cards draw as blank paper with a centered page number — "a map, not a typesetting." Three defects: (1) cards show no text, so the map is unreadable; (2) the page-number labels are invisible in dark mode — they're painted in a label color that resolves light-on-cream (compare the caret-color fix documented in applyAppearance); (3) note markers are placed in the hidden full-width text column's coordinates (ScriptSurface placeNoteMarkers), so in grid they land on whichever card sits at that spot instead of on the note's own page.
Done means: each visible card draws a miniature of its page's real text (at 4-across the type is texture, not reading matter — same taste as Final Draft's panel), the page number is legible on the paper in both light and dark appearances, and a note marker sits on the correct card at the correct scaled height. Grid stays a map: single click selects, double click opens the sheet (existing behavior, keep it). The legacy path and Single/Two-page modes stay byte-for-byte behaviorally unchanged.
Performance is a hard requirement, not a hope: the old comment "Grid must open without snapshotting the script" existed because a 900-page draft must not rasterize 900 bitmaps on open. Render lazily — visible cards only, on scroll — and measure open time on a 100+ page script before and after; report both numbers. Rasterization quality: text must be drawn at the card's scale, not a full-size bitmap downscaled by the layer (that shimmers).
Budget proposal: PageCanvasView.swift, ScriptSurface.swift, NoteMarker if needed, the surface test files, plus docs/MACOS-EXECUTION.md if behavior notes change. Deny: every other package, apple/macOS, apple/iOS, EDraftCore, eDraftEngine, EDraftUI, packages/**, manifests, project files. Proof: swift test --package-path apple/EDraftMacSurface green (currently 296, 5 skipped); new tests pinning (a) marker frames inside the correct card's rect in grid, (b) label/paper contrast in both appearances, (c) visible cards carry rendered content — a rasterize-and-sample test like the probe that diagnosed this; the macOS Debug build passes.